<article class="env-lemma" id="058W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/058W">Lemma <span data-tag="058W">10.84.3</span>.</a> Let $M$ be an $R$-module. Then $M$ is a direct sum of countably generated $R$-modules if and only if it admits a Kaplansky dévissage. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The lemma takes care of the “if” direction. Conversely, suppose $M = \bigoplus _{i \in I} N_ i$ where each $N_ i$ is a countably generated $R$-module. Well-order $I$ so that we can think of it as an ordinal. Then setting $M_ i = \bigoplus _{j < i} N_ j$ gives a Kaplansky dévissage $(M_ i)_{i \in I}$ of $M$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>